 r←Test_Misc_037(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;msg;folder;target;P
⍝ Exercise `ParseDependencySetting` with valid settings in both forms: split into folder and target, no message.
⍝ This is the control for Test_Misc_038.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed
 P←##.Cider.ParseDependencySetting

 ⍝ Empty: no such folder
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.tatin'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace ⍬
 →T.PassesIf(0=≢msg)∧(0=≢folder)∧0=≢target
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.tatin'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace'tatin' ''
 →T.PassesIf(0=≢msg)∧(0=≢folder)∧0=≢target
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.tatin'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace'tatin' '' 'tatinTarget' ''
 →T.PassesIf(0=≢msg)∧(0=≢folder)∧0=≢target

 ⍝ No target namespace: packages go into the project space
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.tatin'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace'tatin' 'tatin-packages'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'tatin-packages'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢target

 (msg folder target)←'dependencies_dev.tatin'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace'tatin' 'tatin-packages_dev=TestCases'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'tatin-packages_dev'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf'TestCases'≡target

 ⍝ A target below a child of the project space
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.nuget'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace'nuget' 'nuget-packages=Foo.Goo'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'nuget-packages'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf'Foo.Goo'≡target

 ⍝ A folder that is not a direct child of the project folder
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.nuget'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace'nuget' 'deps/nuget=Goo'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'deps/nuget'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf'Goo'≡target

 ⍝ A blank inside a folder name is fine
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.tatin'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace'tatin' 'my packages=Foo'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'my packages'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf'Foo'≡target

 ⍝ The new form: the target comes from "tatinTarget" ("nugetTarget")
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies_dev.tatin'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace'tatin' 'tatin-packages_dev' 'tatinTarget' 'TestCases'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'tatin-packages_dev'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf'TestCases'≡target

 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.tatin'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace'tatin' 'tatin-packages' 'tatinTarget' ''
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'tatin-packages'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢target

 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.nuget'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace'nuget' 'my nuget' 'nugetTarget' 'Foo.Goo'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'my nuget'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf'Foo.Goo'≡target

 ⍝ Both forms at once, naming the same namespace
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.tatin'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace'tatin' 'tatin-packages=Foo.Goo' 'tatinTarget' 'Foo.Goo'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'tatin-packages'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf'Foo.Goo'≡target

 ⍝ "tatinTarget" does not affect "nuget"
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.nuget'P ∆MakeDependencyNamespace'nuget' 'nupkgs=Goo' 'tatinTarget' 'Foo'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'nupkgs'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf'Goo'≡target

 r←T._OK
⍝Done
